Live logcat excerpt (emulator-5562, pid 5575, com.izzes.nears.nears_nears_3631_search_uiux)
Repro: module Search -> query "Round Wheat Bread" -> tap item result -> Add To Cart.
Expected (per NEARS-3631 Analytics AC): search_result_tapped (1-based position) fires from
module Search too; add_to_cart{source:search} dual-fires alongside the legacy
search_add_to_cart. Observed: neither fires from module Search's item-tap/add-to-cart path.

09-18 20:00:14.726  5575  5575 I flutter : 📊 analytics: select_item {item_id: 63, screen: search, item_list_id: search_results, item_list_name: search_results, source: search, index: 0}
09-18 20:00:15.457  5575  5575 I flutter : 📊 analytics: view_item {item_id: 63, item_category: 8, price: 4.0, value: 4.0, screen: search, item_list_id: search_results, item_list_name: search_results, source: search, index: 0}
09-18 20:00:38.414  5575  5575 I flutter : 📊 analytics: add_to_cart {item_id: 63, price: 4.0, quantity: 1, currency: AED, value: 4.0, screen: search, item_list_id: search_results, item_list_name: search_results, source: search, index: 0}
(no search_result_tapped line, no search_add_to_cart line, anywhere in the buffer for this session)

Root cause (source-confirmed):
- UserApp/lib/helper/analytics_service.dart:729 logSearchResultTapped(...) has exactly ONE
  call site: UserApp/lib/features/global_search/widgets/global_module_section_widget.dart:76
  — module Search's own item-tap handlers (UserApp/lib/features/search/,
  UserApp/lib/common/widgets/card_design/item_card.dart) never call it.
- UserApp/lib/features/cart/controllers/cart_controller.dart:2177 gates logSearchAddToCart(...)
  on `_searchOriginItemId == addedItemId`; `markSearchOrigin(...)` (the only setter) is called
  ONLY from global_search/widgets/global_module_section_widget.dart — module Search's own
  add-to-cart path never sets the search-origin flag, so the gate never opens.

For comparison, Global Search's OWN store tap correctly fires the ecommerce-standard event:
